lity at inert primes", "family": "geometry", "sections": ["5.3", "6"], "part": 0, "description": "Divisibility at inert primes", "tone": 9, "light": "oklch(0.493 0.138 149.3)", "dark": "oklch(0.668 0.187 149.3)"}, {"id": "frames", "name": "The Bessel–Poincaré frame", "family": "geometry", "sections": ["7"], "part": 0, "description": "The Bessel–Poincaré frame", "tone": 10, "light": "oklch(0.617 0.145 157.7)", "dark": "oklch(0.792 0.181 157.7)"}, {"id": "cohomology", "name": "Cohomological and congruence bounds", "family": "arithmetic", "sections": ["8"], "part": 0, "description": "Cohomological and congruence bounds", "tone": 11, "light": "oklch(0.361 0.061 198.6)", "dark": "oklch(0.536 0.091 198.6)"}, {"id": "galois", "name": "Galois representations from theta lifts", "family": "arithmetic", "sections": ["8.4"], "part": 0, "description": "Galois representations from theta lifts", "tone": 12, "light": "oklch(0.485 0.083 207.0)", "dark": "oklch(0.660 0.113 207.0)"}, {"id": "hosts", "name": "Host fields and auxiliary characters", "family": "arithmetic", "sections": ["9"], "part": 0, "description": "Host fields and auxiliary characters", "tone": 13, "light": "oklch(0.609 0.107 215.4)", "dark": "oklch(0.784 0.138 215.4)"}, {"id": "literature", "name": "Published inputs and sources", "family": "context", "sections": ["10"], "part": 0, "description": "Published inputs and sources", "tone": 14, "light": "oklch(0.557 0.181 341.7)", "dark": "oklch(0.732 0.181 341.7)"}, {"id": "off-path", "name": "Results outside the final proof", "family": "context", "sections": ["11"], "part": 0, "description": "Results outside the final proof", "tone": 15, "light": "oklch(0.433 0.194 333.3)", "dark": "oklch(0.608 0.200 333.3)"}], "topic_order": ["overview", "formal-verification", "method", "landau", "counts", "scale", "slopes", "periods", "inert-primes", "frames", "cohomology", "galois", "hosts", "literature", "off-path"], "source": {"upstream": {"repository": "https://github.com/vincitamore/riemann-lean-account", "commit": "dd9bfc30bf9fc605251a22aa41004d1e22cc303b", "paper": "https://github.com/vincitamore/riemann-lean-account/blob/dd9bfc30bf9fc605251a22aa41004d1e22cc303b/paper/main.pdf"}, "lean": {"authors": "Levent Alpöge with Claude", "repository": "https://github.com/leanprover-community/riemann-hypothesis", "commit": "8b83d5e7b319ebc7b3be6e59ce3411ba2b09d116"}, "lean_scope": "The whole proof map uses James Shore’s compiled dependency data and displays declarations linked from the paper. A line may represent a chain through declarations omitted from the map. Open a statement’s Graph pane to see its immediate Lean dependencies."}, "about": [{"heading": "Where to start", "paragraphs": ["Start with Statement 2.1, where the authors spell out the Riemann Hypothesis. Section 3 then separates the problem into an analytic half and an arithmetic half. The arithmetic half establishes a bound for a weighted count of prime powers. The analytic half uses the bound to rule out zeros of Dirichlet $L$-functions to the right of the critical line, with a pole exception for the trivial character at $s=1$.", "In Section 4, watch for the two errors $x/m$ and $m$. Here $x$ is the scale of the count and $m$ is the length of the theta-lift chain. Choosing $m$ near $\\sqrt{x}$ balances those terms. The bound on the ranks of the lattices controls the third error term. The windowed Landau theorem is the step from the bound on prime powers to nonvanishing."], "links": [{"label": "Read Statement 2.1 beside its Lean", "href": "?n=rh.result&l=b11474-11623&v=lean&view=pdf&page=4"}, {"label": "Read Section 3, The shape of the proof", "href": "?view=pdf&page=11#pdf-section-3"}, {"label": "Open the whole proof map", "href": "map/"}]}], "documents": [{"id": "paper", "slot": "short", "slug": "", "noun": "paper", "main": true, "pdf_only": true, "title": "The argument of a formal proof of the Riemann Hypothesis", "pdf": {"file": "paper.pdf", "sha256": "802d16e339551439de6fec97308cbd4a88b0dd33c4a8d93265d4a6615c95fc75", "bytes": 1215464}}], "reader": {"publish_receipts": true, "lean": {"owner": "Alpöge’s", "ownerSource": "the pinned Lean community import"}}}
